# Fixtures are pinned to LF so a case's golden means the same thing on every
# checkout. Without this, Git's default core.autocrlf=true rewrites the .md
# fixtures to CRLF on Windows and a line-ending bug in one implementation would
# show up as a mysterious fixture failure instead of a parity failure.
#
# This does NOT reduce coverage of the CRLF path: the repo's own *.md files are
# deliberately left unpinned, so CI's windows-latest job runs both linters over
# a fully CRLF tree every time.
* text eol=lf
